1
00:08:18,750 --> 00:08:24,750
Roger Waters: The Wall is a music, documentary film directed by Roger Waters.

2
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:43,500
A concert film that the former Pink Floyd singer-songwriter made on various tour dates between 2010
and 2013, when he was playing his former group's 1980 double-album in its entirety.

3
00:24:56,250 --> 00:25:02,250
Self - Vocal, Guitar, and Bass, played by Roger Waters.

4
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Self - Guitars, played by Dave Kilminster.

5
00:41:33,750 --> 00:41:39,750
Self - Drums, played by Graham Broad.

6
00:49:52,500 --> 00:49:58,500
Self - Guitars, played by Snowy White.

7
00:58:11,250 --> 00:58:17,250
Self - Keyboards, played by Jon Carin.

8
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
Roger Waters: The Wall is a British concert film by Roger Waters.

9
01:14:48,750 --> 01:14:54,750
Directed by Waters and Sean Evans, it captures
performances of Waters' live tour.

10
01:23:07,500 --> 01:23:13,500
It premiered in the Special Presentations section of the 2014 Toronto
International Film Festival, with Waters and Evans in attendance.

11
01:31:26,250 --> 01:31:32,250
The concert design and execution draws heavily from the original concert of the same
name that followed the release of the Pink Floyd album The Wall (1979).

12
01:39:45,000 --> 01:39:51,000
In addition to the 90 minutes of music, the film also contains interspersed documentary and
interview footage taken from a road trip in Europe, with Waters driving an old Bentley.

13
01:48:03,750 --> 01:48:09,750
Waters is also seen reading from John Berger's introduction to Fear, the
English translation of Gabriel Chevallier's novel, La Peur.

14
01:56:22,500 --> 01:56:28,500
The audio is presented in 7.1.4-channel Dolby Atmos.

15
02:04:41,250 --> 02:04:47,250
The film explores themes of concert, live performance, concert film.
